 LEFT, then UP, etc.\nSo SPACE rotates clockwise: DOWN -> LEFT -> UP -> RIGHT -> DOWN.\nTo go from UP to LEFT, I need to rotate 3 times (UP -> RIGHT -> DOWN -> LEFT) or 1 time counterclockwise (but SPACE is clockwise).\nWait, let me reconsider. If SPACE rotates clockwise:\n- DOWN -> LEFT (90 degrees counterclockwise? That's not clockwise)\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. In a standard coordinate system where row increases downward and col increases rightward:\n- Facing DOWN: hands are below the body (higher row values)\n- Facing LEFT: hands are to the left of the body (lower col values)\n- Facing UP: hands are above the body (lower row values)\n- Facing RIGHT: hands are to the right of the body (higher col values)\nIf SPACE rotates clockwise:\n- DOWN -> LEFT (clockwise from down is left? No, clockwise from down is left in a standard coordinate system where up is north, right is east, down is south, left is west. Clockwise from south (down) is west (left). Yes, that's correct.)\n- LEFT -> UP (clockwise from west is north. Yes.)\n- UP -> RIGHT (clockwise from north is east. Yes.)\n- RIGHT -> DOWN (clockwise from east is south. Yes.)\nSo SPACE rotates clockwise: DOWN -> LEFT -> UP -> RIGHT -> DOWN.\nTo go from UP to LEFT, I need to rotate 3 times (UP -> RIGHT -> DOWN -> LEFT).\nBut wait, I could also rotate counterclockwise by pressing SPACE 3 times (which is the same as rotating clockwise 3 times, since 4 rotations = 360 degrees).\nActually, UP -> RIGHT -> DOWN -> LEFT is 3 clockwise rotations. UP -> LEFT is 1 counterclockwise rotation, which is 3 clockwise rotations.\nSo I need 3 SPACE presses to go from UP to LEFT.\nLet me try that.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Rotate from UP to LEFT (3 clockwise rotations)\naction(['SPACE', 'SPACE', 'SPACE'])\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RES